/-!
# An absolutely minimal causality causally open in the future and not in the past: the half-lit line

Programme target `T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness` (`programme/roadmap.toml:734`; layer 1, no label of
`ETT.tex`). Imports: `Causal.LadderLocal`, `Causal.CurvesExtend` (ETT layer, no model, no CBG module,
transitively). On `ℝ`, the **half-lit line** `halfLightLine` has `≪` empty and `x ≤_U y` iff
`x = y ∈ U`, or `0 ≤ x ≤ y` and `[x, y] ⊆ U`: the spacelike line on `(−∞, 0)`, the lightlike line on
`[0, ∞)`. The auditor's sketch of OQ-67 is confirmed in every part; nothing is refuted.

**`T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness/1-causality`** — `halfLightLine`, every field of `Causality`
discharged; `halfLightLine_le`, `halfLightLine_le_of_neg`, `halfLightLine_le_real`.
**`T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness/2-arc-connected`** — `halfLightLine_causallyArcConnected` (the
affine curve, `halfLightLine_causalCurveOn_affine`); on every open,
`halfLightLine_causallyArcConnectedOn`.
**`T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness/3-absolutely-minimal`** — `halfLightLine_absolutelyMinimal`, and on
every open set for every cover of it, `halfLightLine_absolutelyMinimalOn`.
**`T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness/4-causally-open-future`** — `halfLightLine_causallyOpenFuture`,
`halfLightLine_locallyCausallyOpenFuture`.
**`T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness/5-not-causally-open`** — `halfLightLine_Jminus_Ioo`
(`J⁻_M((1, 2)) = [0, 2)`), `halfLightLine_not_isOpen_Jminus_Ioo`,
`halfLightLine_not_causallyOpenPast`, `halfLightLine_not_causallyOpen`.
**`T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness/6-local`** — `halfLightLine_not_locallyCausallyOpen`; the failure sits
at `0`: no open set containing `0` is causally open in the past
(`halfLightLine_not_causallyOpenPastOn_of_zero_mem`), every open set missing it is
(`halfLightLine_causallyOpenPastOn_of_zero_notMem`).
**`T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness/7-ladder`** — push-up (`halfLightLine_pushUp`), causal, globally
hyperbolic (diamonds `[p, q]` or at most a point), strongly causal with open convex neighbourhoods,
a time function (the identity); not tarentin, no chronal neighbours, not causally plain.
**`T-abs-dec8-minimal-witness/8-separation`** — `halfLightLine_separates_causallyOpen` (the keeper's
conjoined witness), `not_causallyOpen_of_causallyOpenFuture_of_absolutelyMinimal_bare`, its gluing
form `not_causallyOpen_of_causallyOpenFuture_of_absolutelyMinimalOn_bare`,
`not_locallyCausallyOpen_of_causallyOpenFuture_of_absolutelyMinimal_bare`,
`not_causallyOpen_of_causallyArcConnected_bare`; time reversal
`not_dual_causallyOpenFuture_of_absolutelyMinimal_bare`, `halfLightLine_dual_separates`.

> Let $M$ be a topological spacetime. The causality of $M$ is open, and $M$ is causally open, if
> for every open subset $\U$ of $M$ and every open subset $\V\subset \U$ the set $J^+_\U(\V)$ is
> open. (`def:causally_open_spacetime_open`, `ETT.tex:694–697`; read with `J^±` by DEC-8)

> A precausality $(\leq,\ll)$ on $M$ is absolutely minimal if for every open cover
> $(\U_i)_{i\in I}$ the precausality generated by $(\U_i,\leq_{\U_i}, \ll_{\U_i})_{i\in I}$ is
> equal to $(\leq,\ll)$. (`def:topological_space_causality_absolutely`, `ETT.tex:397–399`)

> on ℝ, x ≤_U y iff x = y ∈ U, or 0 ≤ x ≤ y and [x, y] ⊆ U; ≪ empty — absolutely minimal (and
> causally arc-connected), causally open in the future, J⁻((1, 2)) = [0, 2) not open, so that the
> printed J⁺-only causal openness is strictly weaker than DEC-8's two-sided one in either reading of
> defi:causalite — proved, or refuted (`programme/roadmap.toml:735`)

## Hypothesis checklist

| target claim | here |
|---|---|
| a causality (`le_trans` by `[x, y] ∪ [y, z] = [x, z]`, `le_mono` as for the rational line) | ✓ proved, every field |
| causally arc-connected (a constant curve below `0`, the affine curve on `[0, ∞)`) | ✓ proved; only `≤ ⇒ curve` is owed, `curve ⇒ ≤` holds in every spacetime |
| absolutely minimal | ✓ proved through `cor:causalement_connexe_minimal`, and on every open set |
| causally open in the future: `J⁺_U(V)` is `V` plus the points above a point of `V ∩ [0, ∞)` | ✓ proved |
| `J⁻((1, 2)) = [0, 2)` not open | ✓ proved, with `U = ⊤` |
| not locally causally open | ✓ proved directly at `0`, and also implied by absolute minimality |
| GH, SCO, time function, push-up; not tarentin, no chronal neighbours, not plain | ✓ proved |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* **The outcome, as a finding for OQ-67**: the half-lit line is absolutely minimal on every open set
  for every cover, i.e. it satisfies the gluing reading of `defi:causalite` (OQ-18) as well as the
  library's, and it is causally open in the future (`def:causally_open_spacetime_open` as printed)
  and not causally open (DEC-8). So DEC-8's `±` strictly strengthens the notion in either reading,
  among absolutely minimal (indeed causally arc-connected, globally hyperbolic, push-up) causalities.
  The printed notion is not invariant under time reversal (`halfLightLine.dual`).
* **Not tarentin**: the half-lit line says nothing about tarentin spacetimes, the setting of
  `prop:tarentin_topological_spacetime_causality`, whose proof uses `J⁻` of an open set
  (`ETT.tex:745–746`). Whether an absolutely minimal tarentin causality can be causally open in the
  future and not in the past is not settled here.
* `ℝ` is Hausdorff and second countable (mathlib instances), so the line is one of ETT's spacetimes.
  No metric notion is used: the order and the topology of `ℝ` only.
* Name: `halfLightLine`, new, checked unique against `Causal/` and the scaffold.

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
